Download Npcap from npcap.com → install with "WinPcap API-compatible mode" enabled
Download Snort 2.9 for Windows → install to C:\Snort
Navigate to C:\Snort\etc\ → edit snort.conf → update paths for dynamic modules and log directory
Create C:\Snort\rules\local.rules with:

alert icmp any any -> any any (msg:"Ping Detected"; sid:1000001; rev:1;)
alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET any (msg:"Possible Port Scan"; flags:S; threshold:type threshold, track by_src, count 5, seconds 10; sid:1000002; rev:1;)

cd C:\Snort\bin → snort -W → note your network interface number
snort -i 5 -c C:\Snort\etc\snort.conf -A console (replace 5 with your interface number)
From Kali Linux: nmap -sS -T4 <Windows_IP_Address>
Observe alerts appearing in the Snort console
Check log directory for saved logs
